{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793461687913,"sessionID":"ses_e6d5a7eaaffe4FxJQatHmabOOJ","part":{"partID":"prt_192a5946d001vYXm5TGm1Ygaf1","sessionID":"ses_e6d5a7eaaffe4FxJQatHmabOOJ","messageID":"msg_192a589d0001fpj5bRXQb9wOxk","type":"tool","id":"call_01a192a5941a702d8d8caf53752049d4","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/part-3/apps/companion_app/README.md"},"output":"Read file /private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/part-3/apps/companion_app/README.md, lines 1-138\n1: # Halloween TV - Guests — `companion_app`\n2: \n3: Guest app (Android, iOS, Web) for Halloween TV. This is the second Flutter\n4: app in the monorepo alongside `apps/tv_app`. The standing owner gate in\n5: `docs/IMPLEMENTATION-TRACKING.md` (\"no secondary Flutter app without\n6: Joaquin's explicit approval\") was lifted for this run: owner approval for\n7: this companion app was recorded for cycle-6, scoped to a controlled pilot\n8: (see below).\n9: \n10: ## What it does\n11: \n12: Anonymous join + read-only now-playing, nothing else:\n13: \n14: - **Join:** the guest enters the organizer-provisioned `partyId`,\n15:   `deviceId`, and `channelId` (typed fields or a pasted JSON object).\n16:   Identifiers are validated locally for shape only — well-formed never\n17:   means registered. There is no login, no Firebase Auth, no registration,\n18:   and no server round-trip at join time.\n19: - **Now playing:** the app invokes exactly one callable,\n20:   `getCurrentManifest`, with exactly `{partyId, deviceId, channelId}`,\n21:   and renders the latest published lineup (four cameras in `cctvSlots`\n22:   wall order, manifest version, server publication time, last-successful-\n23:   check time). The server decides access at manifest-read time\n24:   (`FORBIDDEN`/`UNAUTHENTICATED` render as denial states).\n25: \n26: Default boot is unconfigured/offline: with no backend selected the app\n27: shows the join screen with a configuration banner and performs no Firebase\n28: initialization and no network traffic. A cloud target is selected only\n29: through an explicit, validated `BackendConfig` (build-time\n30: `--dart-define` values via `BackendConfig.fromEnvironment()` in\n31: `lib/main.dart`, or the documented `config/firebase.json` copy workflow\n32: below).\n33: \n34: ## Controlled-pilot assumption\n35: \n36: Party/device/channel IDs are provisioned out-of-band by the organizer for\n37: a controlled pilot (known guests, known devices). The app treats join input\n38: as untrusted data: extra JSON keys (URLs, endpoints, backend selectors,\n39: auto-submit flags) are ignored and never acted upon.\n40: \n41: ## Bearer-capability disclosure\n42: \n43: The party/device IDs are bearer capabilities: the same registered IDs\n44: that authorize the read-only `getCurrentManifest` call also authorize\n45: server-side ACK and generation callables. **This app never invokes those**\n46: (the invoker rejects every callable name except `getCurrentManifest` and\n47: every payload except exactly `{partyId, deviceId, channelId}`), but anyone\n48: holding a provisioned ID pair could call them from elsewhere. Therefore:\n49: \n50: - Provision **dedicated guest-only device IDs** for companion use.\n51: - **Never reuse the TV's own device identity** for guest joins.\n52: - Treat organizer-distributed join payloads like passwords: share them\n53:   only with the intended guest, and rotate/revoke on the backend if one\n54:   leaks.\n55: \n56: ## Spend and hardening\n57: \n58: - **No live spend from this app:** the only callable it invokes is the\n59:   read-only `getCurrentManifest`. Video-generation testing stays on the\n60:   cheapest preset with explicit owner approval per the standing gates; this\n61:   app cannot trigger generation.\n62: - **Pending owner-gated hardening:** App Check enforcement and an explicit\n63:   organizer pairing/approval step are not implemented in this pass and\n64:   remain owner-gated follow-ups before any wider rollout.\n65: \n66: ## Backend options file\n67: \n68: `config/firebase.example.json` holds `YOUR-` placeholders only. To target\n69: a backend locally, copy it to `config/firebase.json` (git-ignored — never\n70: commit real project IDs, keys, or emulator addresses) and fill in real\n71: values. Placeholder values are rejected as unconfigured (fail closed).\n72: \n73: ## Release signing status\n74: \n75: Release builds currently use the **debug keystore** (Flutter template\n76: default: `signingConfig = signingConfigs.getByName(\"debug\")` in\n77: `android/app/build.gradle.kts`). They are **unsuitable for distribution**.\n78: Before any distribution build, follow `docs/RELEASE-SIGNING.md` (party\n79: keystore, env-gated passwords). No signing changes in this pass.\n80: \n81: ## Guest photo submission (consent-gated, backend-pending)\n82: \n83: Optional flow behind \"Submit a guest photo\" on the now-playing screen:\n84: \n85: - The guest picks a photo, checks an explicit affirmative-consent box, then\n86:   confirms a second \"Review and upload\" dialog. No capability call exists\n87:   before both gates pass (`GuestMediaSession.submit` requires\n88:   `consent && confirmed`; `GuestMediaClient.requestUpload` refuses\n89:   `affirmativeConsent: false` before any network).\n90: - The client then requests an upload capability (`requestGuestUpload`),\n91:   PUTs the bytes with the caller-chosen content type (`image/jpeg` or\n92:   `image/png`, threaded from the picker), and confirms\n93:   (`completeGuestUpload`). Every call carries\n94:   `{partyId, deviceId, channelId}` plus `submissionId` where applicable —\n95:   the backend rejects a missing `channelId` with `INVALID_ARGUMENT`.\n96:   Withdrawal (`withdrawGuestMedia`) returns the terminal status `withdrawn`.\n97:   Each submission keeps its own persisted receipt and withdrawal control,\n98:   so withdrawing one photo never strands another; a saved receipt is\n99:   re-checked on next launch (`recover`). Denied/failed uploads keep the\n100:   photo local and retryable.\n101: - Privacy copy (shown in-app): the photo is transformed for Halloween, may\n102:   appear on the party TV, is processed by the media provider and temporarily\n103:   retained in cloud storage; a copy already downloaded to the TV may not be\n104:   removable while that TV is offline.\n105: \n106: Backend status: the guest-media callables are implemented server-side\n107: (`backend/functions/src/guest_upload.ts`, wired in\n108: `backend/functions/src/index.ts`). `requestGuestUpload` requires\n109: `{partyId, deviceId, channelId, contentType, byteSize,\n110: consent:{accepted:true, textVersion:'v1', purpose:'guest_cameo'}}` (consent\n111: literals pinned in `guest_media_client.dart` against\n112: `backend/functions/src/config.ts`) and mints a per-submission signed PUT\n113: capability bound to a server-assigned object path, returning\n114: `{submissionId, objectPath, uploadUrl, expiresAt, consentRevision}` — the\n115: backend never echoes `contentType`; the PUT uses the caller content type.\n116: `completeGuestUpload`, `getGuestMediaStatus`, and `withdrawGuestMedia`\n117: are scoped by `{partyId, deviceId, channelId, submissionId}`, with\n118: withdrawal terminal at status `withdrawn`. The emulator contract test\n119: (`integration_test/guest_photo_emulator_test.dart`) pins this envelope end\n120: to end; it proceeds through capability issuance and reaches the signed PUT\n121: step, which the Storage emulator refuses with HTTP 501 (no XML-API PUT\n122: route), before any completion.\n123: \n124: ## Getting Started\n125: \n126: - `flutter pub get`\n127: - `flutter analyze`\n128: - `flutter test --concurrency=1`\n129: - Emulator contract (needs local Firebase emulators from `backend/`):\n130:   `STORAGE_BUCKET=demo-halloween-tv.appspot.com firebase --config\n131:   firebase.json emulators:start --only firestore,functions,storage\n132:   --project demo-halloween-tv`, then\n133:   `flutter test --concurrency=1\n134:   integration_test/guest_photo_emulator_test.dart`.\n135:   Skips when the emulators are not reachable.\n136: \n137: Display name is `Halloween TV - Guests` (owner decision 2026-10-30) —\n138: deliberately distinct from the TV app (`Halloween TV`).","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/part-3/apps/companion_app/README.md, lines 1-138\n1: # Halloween TV - Guests — `companion_app`\n2: \n3: Guest app (Android, iOS, Web) for Halloween TV. This is the second Flutter\n4: app in the monorepo alongside `apps/tv_app`. The standing owner gate in\n5: `docs/IMPLEMENTATION-TRACKING.md` (\"no secondary Flutter app without\n6: Joaquin's explicit approval\") was lifted for this run: owner approval for\n7: this companion app was recorded for cycle-6, scoped to a controlled pilot\n8: (see below).\n9: \n10: ## What it does\n11: \n12: Anonymous join + read-only now-playing, nothing else:\n13: \n14: - **Join:** the guest enters the organizer-provisioned `partyId`,\n15:   `deviceId`, and `channelId` (typed fields or a pasted JSON object).\n16:   Identifiers are validated locally for shape only — well-formed never\n17:   means registered. There is no login, no Firebase Auth, no registration,\n18:   and no server round-trip at join time.\n19: - **Now playing:** the app invokes exactly one callable,\n20:   `getCurrentManifest`, with exactly `{partyId, deviceId, channelId}`,\n21:   and renders the latest published lineup (four cameras in `cctvSlots`\n22:   wall order, manifest version, server publication time, last-successful-\n23:   check time). The server decides access at manifest-read time\n24:   (`FORBIDDEN`/`UNAUTHENTICATED` render as denial states).\n25: \n26: Default boot is unconfigured/offline: with no backend selected the app\n27: shows the join screen with a configuration banner and performs no Firebase\n28: initialization and no network traffic. A cloud target is selected