le.json` holds `YOUR-` placeholders only. To target\n69: a backend locally, copy it to `config/firebase.json` (git-ignored — never\n70: commit real project IDs, keys, or emulator addresses) and fill in real\n71: values. Placeholder values are rejected as unconfigured (fail closed).\n72: \n73: ## Release signing status\n74: \n75: Release builds currently use the **debug keystore** (Flutter template\n76: default: `signingConfig = signingConfigs.getByName(\"debug\")` in\n77: `android/app/build.gradle.kts`). They are **unsuitable for distribution**.\n78: Before any distribution build, follow `docs/RELEASE-SIGNING.md` (party\n79: keystore, env-gated passwords). No signing changes in this pass.\n80: \n81: ## Guest photo submission (consent-gated, backend-pending)\n82: \n83: Optional flow behind \"Submit a guest photo\" on the now-playing screen:\n84: \n85: - The guest picks a photo, checks an explicit affirmative-consent box, then\n86:   confirms a second \"Review and upload\" dialog. No capability call exists\n87:   before both gates pass (`GuestMediaSession.submit` requires\n88:   `consent && confirmed`; `GuestMediaClient.requestUpload` refuses\n89:   `affirmativeConsent: false` before any network).\n90: - The client then requests an upload capability (`requestGuestUpload`),\n91:   PUTs the bytes with the caller-chosen content type (`image/jpeg` or\n92:   `image/png`, threaded from the picker), and confirms\n93:   (`completeGuestUpload`). Every call carries\n94:   `{partyId, deviceId, channelId}` plus `submissionId` where applicable —\n95:   the backend rejects a missing `channelId` with `INVALID_ARGUMENT`.\n96:   Withdrawal (`withdrawGuestMedia`) returns the terminal status `withdrawn`.\n97:   Each submission keeps its own persisted receipt and withdrawal control,\n98:   so withdrawing one photo never strands another; a saved receipt is\n99:   re-checked on next launch (`recover`). Denied/failed uploads keep the\n100:   photo local and retryable.\n101: - Privacy copy (shown in-app): the photo is transformed for Halloween, may\n102:   appear on the party TV, is processed by the media provider and temporarily\n103:   retained in cloud storage; a copy already downloaded to the TV may not be\n104:   removable while that TV is offline.\n105: \n106: Backend status: the guest-media callables are implemented server-side\n107: (`backend/functions/src/guest_upload.ts`, wired in\n108: `backend/functions/src/index.ts`). `requestGuestUpload` requires\n109: `{partyId, deviceId, channelId, contentType, byteSize,\n110: consent:{accepted:true, textVersion:'v1', purpose:'guest_cameo'}}` (consent\n111: literals pinned in `guest_media_client.dart` against\n112: `backend/functions/src/config.ts`) and mints a per-submission signed PUT\n113: capability bound to a server-assigned object path, returning\n114: `{submissionId, objectPath, uploadUrl, expiresAt, consentRevision}` — the\n115: backend never echoes `contentType`; the PUT uses the caller content type.\n116: `completeGuestUpload`, `getGuestMediaStatus`, and `withdrawGuestMedia`\n117: are scoped by `{partyId, deviceId, channelId, submissionId}`, with\n118: withdrawal terminal at status `withdrawn`. The emulator contract test\n119: (`integration_test/guest_photo_emulator_test.dart`) pins this envelope end\n120: to end; it proceeds through capability issuance and reaches the signed PUT\n121: step, which the Storage emulator refuses with HTTP 501 (no XML-API PUT\n122: route), before any completion.\n123: \n124: ## Getting Started\n125: \n126: - `flutter pub get`\n127: - `flutter analyze`\n128: - `flutter test --concurrency=1`\n129: - Emulator contract (needs local Firebase emulators from `backend/`):\n130:   `STORAGE_BUCKET=demo-halloween-tv.appspot.com firebase --config\n131:   firebase.json emulators:start --only firestore,functions,storage\n132:   --project demo-halloween-tv`, then\n133:   `flutter test --concurrency=1\n134:   integration_test/guest_photo_emulator_test.dart`.\n135:   Skips when the emulators are not reachable.\n136: \n137: Display name is `Halloween TV - Guests` (owner decision 2026-10-30) —\n138: deliberately distinct from the TV app (`Halloween TV`)."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false,"state":{"itemId":"fc_01a192a5941a702d8d8caf53752049d4"}},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/part-3/apps/companion_app/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793461687405,"end":1793461687913}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793461687914,"sessionID":"ses_e6d5a7eaaffe4FxJQatHmabOOJ","part":{"partID":"prt_192a58caf001V7kwQBXacvpp8p","sessionID":"ses_e6d5a7eaaffe4FxJQatHmabOOJ","messageID":"msg_192a589d0001fpj5bRXQb9wOxk","type":"tool","id":"call_01a192a58c5c74b78261e915538973ae","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/part-3/apps/companion_app/lib/src/companion_app.dart"},"output":"Read file /private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/part-3/apps/companion_app/lib/src/companion_app.dart, lines 1-283\n1: /// Root companion widget: join -> now-playing flow over [GuestSession].\n2: ///\n3: /// Composes the p2 dependencies ([CompanionDependencies.create] resolving a\n4: /// [BackendConfig] with unconfigured/offline default boot — no Firebase\n5: /// init, no network) with the p3 [GuestSession] lifecycle. The join screen\n6: /// collects identifiers; each join scopes its own manifest source from the\n7: /// validated [GuestJoinData] (a [FirebaseTvIdentity] derived from the\n8: /// guest-typed party/device IDs, so they scope the actual callable\n9: /// payload), and the now-playing screen renders the latest published\n10: /// lineup from the session state stream.\n11: ///\n12: /// Production path: no `manifestSource` override means the session reads\n13: /// through the real per-join composition\n14: /// (`CompanionDependencies.manifestSourceForJoin` -> [ManifestConnection] ->\n15: /// callable transport -> mapper -> validator). Test seams: [manifestSource]\n16: /// substitutes ONLY the callable boundary (the\n17: /// `ManifestSource<PlaybackManifest>` port); [firebaseBootstrap] and\n18: /// [invokerOverride] substitute only the Firebase-init and callable-invoker\n19: /// boundaries for emulator/production-path tests; parsing, session\n20: /// transitions, and manifest mapping stay on the real production path.\n21: ///\n22: /// Lifecycle: the state observes app background/foreground transitions and\n23: /// suspends the session on background (subscription cancelled, last-known\n24: /// metadata retained) and resumes with a fresh read on foreground return.\n25: library;\n26: \n27: import 'dart:async';\n28: \n29: import 'package:channel_api/channel_api.dart' show ManifestSource;\n30: import 'package:companion_app/src/bootstrap/companion_dependencies.dart';\n31: import 'package:companion_app/src/config/backend_config.dart';\n32: import 'package:companion_app/src/data/party_join_client.dart';\n33: import 'package:companion_app/src/join/guest_join_data.dart';\n34: import 'package:companion_app/src/session/guest_session.dart';\n35: import 'package:companion_app/src/session/guest_session_state.dart';\n36: import 'package:companion_app/src/join/join_payload_scanner.dart';\n37: import 'package:companion_app/src/ui/join_screen.dart';\n38: import 'package:companion_app/src/ui/now_playing_screen.dart';\n39: import 'package:companion_app/src/ui/guest_photo_screen.dart';\n40: import 'package:companion_app/src/media/guest_photo_picker.dart';\n41: import 'package:companion_app/src/session/guest_media_session.dart';\n42: import 'package:core_foundation/core_foundation.dart' show Clock, SystemClock;\n43: import 'package:core_playlist/core_playlist.dart' show PlaybackManifest;\n44: import 'package:core_ui/core_ui.dart' show CctvTheme;\n45: import 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n46: import 'package:infra_firestore/infra_firestore.dart'\n47:     show FirebaseManifestCallableInvoker;\n48: \n49: /// Root widget of the party companion guest app.\n50: final class CompanionApp extends StatefulWidget {\n51:   const CompanionApp({\n52:     super.key,\n53:     this.config,\n54:     this.manifestSource,\n55:     this.clock,\n56:     this.firebaseBootstrap,\n57:     this.invokerOverride,\n58:     this.partyJoinInvokerOverride,\n59:   });\n60: \n61:   /// Backend configuration override. Defaults to unconfigured/offline boot.\n62:   final BackendConfig? config;\n63: \n64:   /// Test seam: substitutes only the callable-boundary manifest source.\n65:   final ManifestSource<PlaybackManifest>? manifestSource;\n66: \n67:   /// Clock for last-successful-check timestamps.\n68:   final Clock? clock;\n69: \n70:   /// Test/emulator seam: substitutes only the Firebase-init boundary.\n71:   final FirebaseBootstrap? firebaseBootstrap;\n72: \n73:   /// Test/emulator seam: substitutes only the callable-invoker boundary.\n74:   final FirebaseManifestCallableInvoker? invokerOverride;\n75:   final PartyJoinCallableInvoker? partyJoinInvokerOverride;\n76: \n77:   @override\n78:   State<CompanionApp> createState() => _CompanionAppState();\n79: }\n80: \n81: final class _CompanionAppState extends State<CompanionApp>\n82:     with WidgetsBindingObserver {\n83:   GuestSession? _session;\n84:   StreamSubscription<GuestSessionState>? _statesSubscription;\n85:   CompanionDependencies? _baseDependencies;\n86:   BackendConfig? _resolvedConfig;\n87:   String? _unavailableReason;\n88:   bool _booted = false;\n89: \n90:   @override\n91:   void initState() {\n92:     super.initState();\n93:     WidgetsBinding.instance.addObserver(this);\n94:     _boot();\n95:   }\n96: \n97:   Future<void> _boot() async {\n98:     final Clock clock = widget.clock ?? const SystemClock();\n99:     final ManifestSource<PlaybackManifest>? override = widget.manifestSource;\n100:     if (override != null) {\n101:       final GuestSession session = GuestSession(source: override, clock: clock);\n102:       _attach(session);\n103:       if (!mounted) {\n104:         await session.dispose();\n105:         return;\n106:       }\n107:       setState(() {\n108:         _session = session;\n109:         _booted = true;\n110:       });\n111:       return;\n112:     }\n113:     final BackendConfig resolved =\n114:         widget.config ?? BackendConfig.unconfigured();\n115:     _resolvedConfig = resolved;\n116:     final CompanionDependencies dependencies =\n117:         await CompanionDependencies.create(\n118:           config: resol