al callable payload; the [channelId] scopes\n68:   /// the requested document. Identity construction is deferred to the\n69:   /// first [ManifestSource.watchCurrent] call so an identifier the guest\n70:   /// parser accepts but the backend identity shape rejects surfaces as a\n71:   /// session `invalidData` error (via [ManifestFailure.classify]) instead\n72:   /// of throwing out of the join wiring. When no live invoker is available\n73:   /// (offline/unconfigured), returns the base [manifestSource] so the\n74:   /// existing recoverable reason still surfaces.\n75:   ManifestSource<PlaybackManifest> manifestSourceForJoin(GuestJoinData join) {\n76:     final FirebaseManifestCallableInvoker? invoker = _invoker;\n77:     if (invoker == null) {\n78:       return manifestSource;\n79:     }\n80:     return _JoinScopedSource(join: join, invoker: invoker);\n81:   }\n82: \n83:   static Future<CompanionDependencies> create({\n84:     BackendConfig? config,\n85:     FirebaseTvIdentity? identity,\n86:     FirebaseBootstrap? firebaseBootstrap,\n87:     FirebaseFunctions? functionsOverride,\n88:     FirebaseManifestCallableInvoker? invokerOverride,\n89:     PartyJoinCallableInvoker? partyJoinInvokerOverride,\n90:   }) async {\n91:     final BackendConfig resolved = config ?? BackendConfig.unconfigured();\n92:     if (!resolved.isLiveConfigured) {\n93:       return CompanionDependencies._(\n94:         config: resolved,\n95:         manifestSource: _UnavailableManifestSource(\n96:           ManifestFailure.configuration(\n97:             resolved.error ?? 'backend is not configured',\n98:           ),\n99:         ),\n100:         identity: identity,\n101:         remoteUnavailableReason: resolved.error ?? 'backend is not configured',\n102:         invoker: null,\n103:         partyJoinClient: null,\n104:         guestMediaClient: null,\n105:       );\n106:     }\n107:     if (identity == null) {\n108:       // Live backend selected but no fixed identity: this is the normal\n109:       // pre-join state. Firebase is still initialized now (so init failures\n110:       // surface pre-join as recoverable state) and the invoker is built;\n111:       // each join scopes its own source through [manifestSourceForJoin].\n112:       try {\n113:         await (firebaseBootstrap ?? _initializeFirebase)(resolved);\n114:         FirebaseFunctions? functions;\n115:         FirebaseFunctions resolveFunctions() =>\n116:             functions ??= _configuredFunctions(resolved, functionsOverride);\n117:         final FirebaseManifestCallableInvoker invoker;\n118:         if (invokerOverride != null) {\n119:           invoker = invokerOverride;\n120:         } else {\n121:           invoker = CallableManifestInvoker(functions: resolveFunctions());\n122:         }\n123:         return CompanionDependencies._(\n124:           config: resolved,\n125:           manifestSource: _UnscopedManifestSource(),\n126:           identity: null,\n127:           remoteUnavailableReason: null,\n128:           invoker: invoker,\n129:           guestMediaClient: GuestMediaClient(\n130:             invoker: CallableGuestMediaInvoker(resolveFunctions),\n131:             transport: HttpGuestMediaTransport(),\n132:           ),\n133:           partyJoinClient: PartyJoinClient(\n134:             invoker:\n135:                 partyJoinInvokerOverride ??\n136:                 CallablePartyJoinInvoker(functions: resolveFunctions()),\n137:           ),\n138:         );\n139:       } on Object catch (error) {\n140:         final ManifestFailure failure = ManifestFailure.classify(error);\n141:         return CompanionDependencies._(\n142:           config: resolved,\n143:           manifestSource: _UnavailableManifestSource(failure),\n144:           identity: null,\n145:           remoteUnavailableReason:\n146:               'Firebase could not be initialized: ${failure.message}',\n147:           invoker: null,\n148:           partyJoinClient: null,\n149:           guestMediaClient: null,\n150:         );\n151:       }\n152:     }\n153:     try {\n154:       await (firebaseBootstrap ?? _initializeFirebase)(resolved);\n155:       FirebaseFunctions? functions;\n156:       FirebaseFunctions resolveFunctions() =>\n157:           functions ??= _configuredFunctions(resolved, functionsOverride);\n158:       final FirebaseManifestCallableInvoker invoker;\n159:       if (invokerOverride != null) {\n160:         invoker = invokerOverride;\n161:       } else {\n162:         invoker = CallableManifestInvoker(functions: resolveFunctions());\n163:       }\n164:       return CompanionDependencies._(\n165:         config: resolved,\n166:         manifestSource: ManifestConnection(\n167:           identity: identity,\n168:           invoker: invoker,\n169:         ),\n170:         identity: identity,\n171:         remoteUnavailableReason: null,\n172:         invoker: invoker,\n173:         guestMediaClient: GuestMediaClient(\n174:           invoker: CallableGuestMediaInvoker(resolveFunctions),\n175:           transport: HttpGuestMediaTransport(),\n176:         ),\n177:         partyJoinClient: PartyJoinClient(\n178:           invoker:\n179:               partyJoinInvokerOverride ??\n180:               CallablePartyJoinInvoker(functions: resolveFunctions()),\n181:         ),\n182:       );\n183:     } on Object catch (error) {\n184:       final ManifestFailure failure = ManifestFailure.classify(error);\n185:       return CompanionDependencies._(\n186:         config: resolved,\n187:         manifestSource: _UnavailableManifestSource(failure),\n188:         identity: identity,\n189:         remoteUnavailableReason:\n190:             'Firebase could not be initialized: ${failure.message}',\n191:         invoker: null,\n192:         partyJoinClient: null,\n193:         guestMediaClient: null,\n194:       );\n195:     }\n196:   }\n197: \n198:   static Future<void> _initializeFirebase(BackendConfig config) async {\n199:     if (Firebase.apps.isEmpty) {\n200:       await Firebase.initializeApp(options: config.firebaseOptions!);\n201:     }\n202:   }\n203: \n204:   static FirebaseFunctions _configuredFunctions(\n205:     BackendConfig config,\n206:     FirebaseFunctions? override,\n207:   ) {\n208:     final FirebaseFunctions functions =\n209:         override ??\n210:         FirebaseFunctions.instanceFor(region: config.functionsRegion);\n211:     if (config.useEmulator) {\n212:       functions.useFunctionsEmulator(\n213:         config.functionsEmulatorHost,\n214:         config.functionsEmulatorPort!,\n215:       );\n216:     }\n217:     return functions;\n218:   }\n219: }\n220: \n221: final class _UnavailableManifestSource\n222:     implements ManifestSource<PlaybackManifest> {\n223:   _UnavailableManifestSource(this.failure);\n224: \n225:   final ManifestFailure failure;\n226: \n227:   @override\n228:   Stream<PlaybackManifest> watchCurrent({\n229:     required String partyId,\n230:     required String channelId,\n231:   }) => Stream<PlaybackManifest>.error(\n232:     ManifestTransportException('remote manifest is unavailable', failure),\n233:   );\n234: }\n235: \n236: /// Placeholder source for a live-but-unscoped composition (pre-join).\n237: ///\n238: /// The app never reads through this: every join scopes its own source via\n239: /// [CompanionDependencies.manifestSourceForJoin]. Surfacing here means a\n240: /// programming error (reading before a join bound an identity).\n241: final class _UnscopedManifestSource\n242:     implements ManifestSource<PlaybackManifest> {\n243:   @override\n244:   Stream<PlaybackManifest> watchCurrent({\n245:     required String partyId,\n246:     required String channelId,\n247:   }) => Stream<PlaybackManifest>.error(\n248:     StateError('join a party before reading the manifest'),\n249:   );\n250: }\n251: \n252: /// Per-join scoped source: derives the [FirebaseTvIdentity] from validated\n253: /// [GuestJoinData] so the guest-typed IDs scope the actual callable\n254: /// payload, then delegates to a real [ManifestConnection].\n255: ///\n256: /// Identity construction is deferred to the first `watchCurrent` call so an\n257: /// identifier the guest parser accepts but the backend identity shape\n258: /// rejects surfaces as a session `invalidData` error (the session's\n259: /// subscribe path funnels synchronous `watchCurrent` throws through\n260: /// [ManifestFailure.classify]) instead of throwing out of the join wiring.\n261: final class _JoinScopedSource implements ManifestSource<PlaybackManifest> {\n262:   _JoinScopedSource({required GuestJoinData join, required this.invoker})\n263:     : _join = join;\n264: \n265:   final GuestJoinData _join;\n266:   final FirebaseManifestCallableInvoker invoker;\n267: \n268:   @override\n269:   Stream<PlaybackManifest> watchCurrent({\n270:     required String partyId,\n271:     required String channelId,\n272:   }) {\n273:     final ManifestConnection connection = ManifestConnection(\n274:       identity: FirebaseTvIdentity(\n275:         partyId: _join.partyId.value,\n276:         deviceId: _join.deviceId.value,\n277:       ),\n278:       invoker: invoker,\n279:     );\n280:     return connection.watchCurrent(partyId: partyId, channelId: channelId);\n281:   }\n282: }","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/part-3/apps/companion_app/lib/src/bootstrap/companion_dependencies.dart, lines 1-282\n1: /// Composition root wiring config -> connection -> `ManifestSource`.\n2: ///\n3: /// [CompanionDependencies.create] resolves a [BackendConfig] (defaulting to\n4: /// unconfigured/offline boot), initializes Firebase only when a cloud\n5: /// target was explicitly selected and validated, and exposes a\n6: /// `channel_api` `ManifestSource<PlaybackManifest>` backed by the real\n7: /// callable transport. Invalid config or init failure resolves to a\n8: /// recoverable [remoteUnavailableReason] with an erroring manifest source;\n9: